{
  "key": "yield_relationships",
  "title": "Yield Relationships & Bond Math",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Core Yield Definitions",
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "Nominal Yield (Coupon Rate) = stated annual coupon \u00f7 par ($1,000). Fixed at issuance; never changes.",
        "Current Yield (CY) = Annual Coupon Income \u00f7 Current Market Price. Ignores gain/loss to maturity.",
        "Yield to Maturity (YTM) = total annualized return if held to maturity, assuming all coupons reinvested at YTM and bond redeemed at par. Reflects coupon + amortization of premium / accretion of discount.",
        "Yield to Call (YTC) = total annualized return if bond is called at the first/next call date at the call price. Uses call price (often par or par + premium) and shorter time horizon.",
        "Yield to Worst (YTW) = lower of YTM or YTC \u2014 what must be disclosed to customer on a callable bond."
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Price / Yield Relationship (INVERSE)",
      "type": "table",
      "items": [
        {
          "Bond Trading At": "Discount (Price < Par)",
          "Coupon": "Lowest",
          "Current Yield": "Higher than coupon",
          "YTM": "Higher than CY",
          "YTC": "Higher than YTM",
          "Order (low\u2192high)": "Coupon < CY < YTM < YTC"
        },
        {
          "Bond Trading At": "Par (Price = $1,000)",
          "Coupon": "=",
          "Current Yield": "= Coupon",
          "YTM": "= Coupon",
          "YTC": "= Coupon",
          "Order (low\u2192high)": "All equal"
        },
        {
          "Bond Trading At": "Premium (Price > Par)",
          "Coupon": "Highest",
          "Current Yield": "Lower than coupon",
          "YTM": "Lower than CY",
          "YTC": "Lower than YTM (YTW)",
          "Order (low\u2192high)": "YTC < YTM < CY < Coupon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Key Formulas",
      "type": "formula",
      "items": [
        "Current Yield = Annual Coupon $ / Market Price",
        "Approx YTM \u2248 [Annual Coupon + (Par \u2212 Price)/Years to Maturity] \u00f7 [(Par + Price)/2]",
        "Approx YTC \u2248 [Annual Coupon + (Call Price \u2212 Price)/Years to Call] \u00f7 [(Call Price + Price)/2]",
        "Tax-Equivalent Yield (TEY) = Muni Yield \u00f7 (1 \u2212 Investor's Marginal Federal Tax Rate)",
        "After-Tax Yield (taxable bond) = Taxable Yield \u00d7 (1 \u2212 Tax Rate)",
        "Total Return = (Income + Capital Gain) / Cost Basis"
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Bond Pricing Conventions \u2014 Points & Basis Points",
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "1 bond point = 1% of par = $10 (par = $1,000). A bond quoted at 102 = $1,020; at 98 = $980.",
        "Quotes in 1/8ths (corporates): 101 1/8 = $1,011.25; each 1/8 pt = $1.25.",
        "Treasury notes/bonds quoted in 32nds: 99-16 = 99 + 16/32 = 99.50% of par = $995.00. Each 1/32 = $0.3125.",
        "T-bills quoted on discount yield basis (not price).",
        "1 basis point (bp) = 0.01% = 1/100 of 1%. 100 bps = 1.00%. A yield move from 4.25% \u2192 4.50% = +25 bps."
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Accrued Interest Conventions (post-5/28/2024 T+1)",
      "type": "table",
      "items": [
        {
          "Security": "Corporate bonds",
          "Day-Count": "30/360 (assume 30-day months, 360-day year)",
          "Settlement": "T+1",
          "Accrues": "From last coupon date up to but NOT including settlement"
        },
        {
          "Security": "Municipal bonds",
          "Day-Count": "30/360",
          "Settlement": "T+1 (MSRB G-12/G-15, eff. 5/28/2024)",
          "Accrues": "Last coupon \u2192 day before settlement"
        },
        {
          "Security": "U.S. Treasury notes/bonds",
          "Day-Count": "Actual/Actual (actual days / actual days in coupon period)",
          "Settlement": "T+1",
          "Accrues": "Last coupon \u2192 day before settlement"
        },
        {
          "Security": "T-bills / zero-coupons",
          "Day-Count": "No accrued interest (no coupon)",
          "Settlement": "T+1",
          "Accrues": "N/A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "YTC vs YTM \u2014 Which Governs?",
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "Issuers CALL when rates fall \u2192 premium bonds are most likely to be called \u2192 YTC is the binding (worst-case) yield.",
        "Discount bonds: issuer unlikely to call (would refinance at higher cost) \u2192 YTM is the relevant yield.",
        "FINRA confirms (Rule 2232 / customer confirmation context) that yield-to-worst is the figure disclosed when lower than YTM.",
        "YTC uses (a) shorter time to call and (b) the call price \u2014 not par \u2014 in the formula."
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Tax-Equivalent Yield \u2014 Quick Reference",
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "Use TEY to compare a tax-exempt muni to a taxable corporate/Treasury at the investor's marginal bracket.",
        "Example: 4% muni, 32% bracket \u2192 TEY = 4% / (1 \u2212 0.32) = 4% / 0.68 = 5.88%.",
        "Treasuries: exempt from STATE/LOCAL tax only \u2014 taxable federally. Use after-tax yield comparisons accordingly.",
        "Municipal interest is federally tax-exempt (taxable munis like BABs are exception)."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "common_traps": [
    "Reversing the inverse relationship: when PRICE goes UP, YIELD goes DOWN \u2014 and vice versa. A 'higher yield' bond is the cheaper bond.",
    "Forgetting that on a PREMIUM callable bond the YTC is the LOWEST yield and is the yield-to-worst that must be quoted to the customer. On a DISCOUNT bond, YTM is lowest/relevant.",
    "Confusing point values: 1 point = $10 (not $1). 1 basis point = $0.10 per $1,000 par per year of yield \u2014 not a dollar price move.",
    "Mixing day-count conventions: corporates AND munis use 30/360; Treasuries use actual/actual. Don't apply 30/360 to a T-note accrued interest question.",
    "Using PAR instead of CALL PRICE in the YTC numerator, or using years-to-maturity instead of years-to-call. YTC must use the call price and the call date.",
    "Forgetting tax-equivalent yield works ONLY for federal tax-exempt munis; do not gross up a Treasury yield (Treasuries are federally taxable)."
  ],
